rm=linux-x86_64 manifest=host/gambit/ffi/TOOLCHAIN.linux-x86_64.sha256\n81:gambitffi: recorded 7 toolchain inputs\n86:and finish the toolchain portion with `gambitffi: toolchain verified (7 inputs)`.\n107:with `python3 host/gambit/ffi/test-toolchain.py` (set TMPDIR inside the checkout\n.github/actions/setup-chez/action.yml\n.github/workflows/tests.yml\n#!/bin/sh\n# External deadline kills the entire gate process group, including make's children.\nexec python3 - \"$@\" <<'PY'\nimport os, signal, subprocess, sys\nseconds = float(sys.argv[1])\np = subprocess.Popen(sys.argv[2:], start_new_session=True)\ntry:\n    status = p.wait(timeout=seconds)\nexcept subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n    os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n    p.wait()\n    print('WATCHDOG: TIMEOUT after %ss: %s' % (seconds, ' '.join(sys.argv[2:])), file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(124)\nsys.exit(status if status >= 0 else 128 - status)\nPY\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat .github/actions/setup-chez/action.yml; sed -n '95,145p' .github/workflows/tests.yml; rg -n 'gambit|bionic-ci' ci/termux* Makefile; cat host/gambit/ffi/test-toolchain.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat .github/actions/setup-chez/action.yml; sed -n '95,145p' .github/workflows/tests.yml; rg -n 'gambit|bionic-ci' ci/termux* Makefile; cat host/gambit/ffi/test-toolchain.py\"","aggregated_output":"name: Set up Chez, Gambit and the certify oracle\ndescription: >-\n  The toolchain the jolt gate runs on: the pinned Chez Scheme built from source\n  with jolt's kernel patches (on PATH as chez), Gambit for the host/gambit\n  gates, and JDK 21 plus the Clojure CLI as the conformance oracle. Chez and\n  Gambit come from the actions cache when the key matches, so a warm run spends\n  seconds here. Every shard of the gate job runs this, which is why it is one\n  action and not steps copied per job.\nruns:\n  using: composite\n  steps:\n    # The runner image's OS id (ubuntu24), for the cache keys. ImageOS is a\n    # process env var, not one the workflow set, so ${{ env.ImageOS }} was\n    # always empty and the keys read chez-Linux--v10.4.1-…: a cache built on\n    # ubuntu-24.04 would have been restored on 26.04. Read from the shell, it\n    # is there, so the first run on each image builds Chez and Gambit once.\n    - id: image\n      shell: bash\n      run: echo \"os=$ImageOS\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n    # Build Chez from source rather than the distro package: the apt\n    # chezscheme ships petite+scheme only, with no kernel dev files\n    # (libkernel.a, scheme.h), so `jolt build` (the buildsmoke gate) can't link\n    # a binary and would skip. The source build provides them, plus the libs the\n    # kernel links against.\n    - name: Install build dependencies\n      shell: bash\n      run: |\n        sudo apt-get update\n        sudo apt-get install -y build-essential git liblz4-dev zlib1g-dev libncurses-dev uuid-dev\n\n    - name: Cache Chez Scheme\n      id: cache-chez\n      uses: actions/cache@v5\n      with:\n        path: /opt/chez\n        key: chez-${{ runner.os }}-${{ steps.image.outputs.os }}-v10.4.1-x11off-pic-${{ hashFiles('host/chez/chez-patches/*.patch') }}\n\n    - name: Build Chez Scheme from source\n      if: steps.cache-chez.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n      shell: bash\n      run: |\n        git clone --depth 1 --branch v10.4.1 https://github.com/cisco/ChezScheme.git /tmp/chez-src\n        sh \"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/ci/apply-chez-patches.sh\" /tmp/chez-src\n        cd /tmp/chez-src\n        # --disable-x11: the expression editor's X11 clipboard isn't needed and\n        # would pull an X11 build/link dep.\n        #\n        # CFLAGS+=-fPIC: `jolt build --library` links Chez's libkernel.a into a\n        # shared object, which a kernel built without -fPIC cannot do — the\n        # -shared link fails with a relocation error. build-lib-smoke.sh treats\n        # that as an environment limitation and SKIPS, so without this flag the\n        # buildlibsmoke gate passes without testing anything.\n        ./configure --installprefix=/opt/chez --threads --disable-x11 CFLAGS+=-fPIC\n        make -j\"$(nproc)\"\n        sudo make install\n        sudo chown -R \"$USER\" /opt/chez\n\n    - name: Put chez on PATH\n      shell: bash\n      run: |\n        # Installed as `scheme`; the gate invokes `chez`. A wrapper that execs\n        # scheme keeps argv0 so Chez finds its boot files. Placed next to scheme\n        # so build.ss derives the csv dir (libkernel.a/scheme.h) from it.\n        printf '#!/bin/sh\\nexec /opt/chez/bin/scheme \"$@\"\\n' > /opt/chez/bin/chez\n        chmod +x /opt/chez/bin/chez\n        echo '/opt/chez/bin' >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"\n        /opt/chez/bin/chez --version\n\n    # Gambit, for the host/gambit gates (gambitcheck/kernel/eval/boot/unbound/\n    # vars/profile). apt's gambc is 4.9.3; the gates run on 4.9.8, the brew\n    # pin, so build the tag from source and cache it like Chez. The git tag\n    # ships the generated C files, so no bootstrap compiler is involved.\n    # Flags are the brew formula's minus openssl, which nothing here uses:\n    # --enable-single-host is the one-C-file-per-module build, the runtime\n    # options make UTF-8 the default encoding on files, stdio and terminals.\n    - name: Cache Gambit\n      id: cache-gambit\n      uses: actions/cache@v5\n      with:\n        path: /opt/gambit\n        key: gambit-${{ runner.os }}-${{ steps.image.outputs.os }}-v4.9.8-single-host-f8\n\n    - name: Build Gambit from source\n      if: steps.cache-gambit.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n      shell: bash\n      run: |\n        git clone --depth 1 --branch v4.9.8 https://github.com/gambit/gambit.git /tmp/gambit-src\n        cd /tmp/gambit-src\n        ./configure --prefix=/opt/gambit --enable-single-host --enable-default-runtime-options=f8,-8,t8\n        make -j\"$(nproc)\"\n        sudo make install\n        sudo chown -R \"$USER\" /opt/gambit\n\n    - name: Show Gambit version\n      # Not on PATH: `gsc` is Ghostscript's name too, and the Makefile only\n      # ever runs $(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/bin/gsi and gsc.\n      shell: bash\n      run: /opt/gambit/bin/gsi -v\n\n    # The oracle Clojure (test/conformance/profile.edn :clojure-version) and\n    # its spec deps, from the actions cache: every shard of every run used to\n    # fetch them cold from Maven Central, and Central's 429s outlasted the five\n    # retries below (#1706's shard 1/4, 2026-11-17). A release version is never\n    # re-checked once it is in ~/.m2, so a hit makes no request at all. Saved\n    # right after the resolve, before any gate can add to ~/.m2.\n    - name: Restore the oracle Clojure\n      id: cache-oracle-clojure\n      uses: actions/cache/restore@v5\n      with:\n        path: ~/.m2/repository\n        key: oracle-clojure-${{ hashFiles('test/conformance/profile.edn') }}\n\n    - name: Install JDK + Clojure (certify oracle)\n      shell: bash\n      run: |\n        # openjdk-21 by name, not default-jdk: the corpus is measured on JDK 21\n        # (test/conformance/profile.edn :oracle-jdk), and default-jdk follows\n        # the image, so it is 25 on ubuntu-26.04 and certify refuses the oracle.\n        sudo apt-get install -y openjdk-21-jdk-headless rlwrap\n        jdk=/usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk-$(dpkg --print-architecture)\n        # --retry + --fail so a transient CDN error retries instead of handing\n        # bash an HTML error page (a 2min timeout page flaked a run)\n        curl --fail --retry 5 --retry-delay 10 --retry-all-errors -L -O \\\n          https://github.com/clojure/brew-install/releases/latest/download/linux-install.sh\n        head -1 linux-install.sh | grep -q '^#!' || { echo \"installer download corrupt\"; cat linux-install.sh | head -5; exit 1; }\n        sudo bash linux-install.sh\n        # The runner image puts an older Temurin's java first on PATH, and the\n        # clojure launcher runs that (JAVA_HOME is only its fallback when no\n        # java is on PATH). JAVA_CMD is the launcher's first choice: point it\n        # at the JDK just installed (the corpus is measured on the JDK\n        # test/conformance/profile.edn pins as :oracle-jdk, and certify.clj\n        # refuses any other).\n        echo \"JAVA_CMD=$jdk/bin/java\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n        echo \"JAVA_HOME=$jdk\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n        clojure --version\n        # Resolve the Clojure certify runs, test/conformance/profile.edn's\n        # :clojure-version, not the launcher's default: the default follows the\n        # `latest` installer above, nothing gates on it, and a release can reach\n        # the installer before its jar reaches Maven Central (1.12.6 came back\n        # \"absent\" on one shard). Resolving the pinned one here leaves it in\n        # ~/.m2 for certify, so the gate makes no Maven fetch of its own. And\n        # retried, because every shard of every run fetches it cold and Central\n        # answers that with a 429 now and then.\n        v=$(sed -n 's/^ :clojure-version \"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' test/conformance/profile.edn)\n        [ -n \"$v\" ] || { echo \"no :clojure-version in test/conformance/profile.edn\"; exit 1; }\n        deps=\"{:deps {org.clojure/clojure {:mvn/version \\\"$v\\\"}}}\"\n        for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do\n          JAVA_CMD=$jdk/bin/java clojure -Sdeps \"$deps\" -M -e '(println \"oracle Clojure\" (clojure-version) \"on JDK\" (System/getProperty \"java.runtime.version\"))' && break\n          [ \"$i\" -lt 5 ] || exit 1\n          echo \"resolving Clojure $v failed (attempt $i of 5), retrying\"\n          sleep $((i * 15))\n        done\n\n    - name: Save the oracle Clojure\n      if: steps.cache-oracle-clojure.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n      uses: actions/cache/save@v5\n      with:\n        path: ~/.m2/repository\n        key: oracle-clojure-${{ hashFiles('test/conformance/profile.edn') }}\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04-arm\n    timeout-minutes: 90\n    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      matrix:\n        shard: [1, 2, 3]\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v5\n        with:\n          submodules: recursive\n      - name: Month (Termux image cache key)\n        id: month\n        run: echo \"month=$(date -u +%Y-%m)\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n      # The image comes from the cache, not Docker Hub, when it can: anonymous\n      # pulls from the shared runners hit Docker Hub's rate limit (ci/pull-image.sh).\n      - name: Restore Termux image\n        id: termux-image\n        uses: actions/cache/restore@v5\n        with:\n          path: ~/termux-image.tar\n          key: termux-docker-aarch64-${{ steps.month.outputs.month }}\n      - name: Pull Termux image\n        run: sh ci/pull-image.sh termux/termux-docker:aarch64 \"$HOME/termux-image.tar\"\n      - name: Save Termux image\n        if: steps.termux-image.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n        uses: actions/cache/save@v5\n        with:\n          path: ~/termux-image.tar\n          key: termux-docker-aarch64-${{ steps.month.outputs.month }}\n      # Keyed on what decides the build: the makes pin (which names the Chez\n      # version), the provisioning script and jolt's kernel patches.\n      - name: Bionic Chez cache key\n        id: bionic-chez\n        run: echo \"key=bionic-chez-$(sed -n 's/^V := //p' Makefile)-${{ hashFiles('host/chez/provision-chez.sh', 'host/chez/chez-patches/*.patch') }}\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n      - name: Restore bionic Chez\n        id: bionic-chez-cache\n        uses: actions/cache/restore@v5\n        with:\n          path: .cache/local\n          key: ${{ steps.bionic-chez.outputs.key }}\n      - name: Build and gate jolt in Termux (shard ${{ matrix.shard }}/3)\n        run: |\n          mkdir -p target/release\n          chmod 777 target target/release\n          docker run --rm --entrypoint /system/bin/sh -v \"$PWD\":/src \\\n            termux/termux-docker:aarch64 \\\n            -c 'mkdir -p /tmp && chmod 1777 /tmp && exec /entrypoint.sh sh /src/ci/termux-build.sh ci-shard SHARD-SET=ci SHARD=${{ matrix.shard }} SHARDS=3'\n      - name: Stage bionic Chez for the cache\n        if: steps.bionic-chez-cache.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n        run: |\n          rm -rf .cache/local\nMakefile:128:.PHONY: nsaudit kondocheck build install test ci bionic-ci ci-shard ci-shard-list gate-run-test gate-run-ci gate-run-bionic-ci gate-run-ci-shard gate-status hooks attributioncheck noticecheck monitormodel \\\nMakefile:129:        gambitcheck gambitkernel gambiteval gambitseed gambitweb gambitprofile \\\nMakefile:130:        gambitgen gambitgencheck gambitseedcheck gambitunbound gambitunbound-regen \\\nMakefile:131:        gambitffi gambitffi-abi gambitffi-errno-check gambitffi-load-failure-smoke gambitffi-bridge \\\nMakefile:132:        gambitvars gambitvars-regen gambitstatics gambitstatics-regen gambittwins grenadinecheck \\\nMakefile:189:  certify gambitcheck gambitkernel gambitgencheck gambitseedcheck gambitboot gambiteval gambitunbound gambitvars gambitstatics gambittwins gambitprofile grenadinecheck fibers fiberspoll gosm asynctimer ticks interruptnest monitorescape windescape threadsafety maskedacquire ioerrno cas flow\nMakefile:263:bionic-ci:\nMakefile:264:\t$(call run-gate,bionic-ci,$(CI-GATES))\nMakefile:288:gate-run-bionic-ci: $(filter-out $(QUIET-GATES),$(CI-GATES))\nMakefile:292:# (selfhost plus CI-GATES) or ci (CI-GATES alone, what bionic-ci runs), and\nMakefile:1449:# The two hand-mirrored host file pairs (chez/rt.ss <-> gambit/rt-core.ss and the\nMakefile:1851:# Where the gambit gates find gsi and gsc: GAMBIT_PREFIX/bin, brew's\nMakefile:1852:# gambit-scheme prefix by default (tests.yml builds 4.9.8 from source into\nMakefile:1853:# /opt/gambit and passes GAMBIT_PREFIX=/opt/gambit). NEVER bare gsc/gsi (gsc on\nMakefile:1854:# PATH is Ghostscript): always a prefix's binary. Absolute, because gambitboot\nMakefile:1855:# and unbound-check.sh cd into host/gambit before running it.\nMakefile:1856:GAMBIT_PREFIX ?= $(shell brew --prefix gambit-scheme 2>/dev/null)\nMakefile:1860:# Every gambit gate is detection-gated like certify: no gambit, clean skip. With\nMakefile:1863:# no-ops that read as green (the boot ran dead for two weeks with every gambit\nMakefile:1866:\t  echo \"$@: no gambit at $(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/bin and JOLT_REQUIRE_GAMBIT is set\" >&2; exit 1; \\\nMakefile:1868:\t  echo \"$@: gambit-scheme not installed (GAMBIT_PREFIX=$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)) — skipped\"; \\\nMakefile:1871:# Gambit adapter gate (G1, jolt-mj95.2): loads host/gambit/{prelude-shims,\nMakefile:1875:# host/gambit/records-gambit.ss is GENERATED from the four host/chez records\nMakefile:1879:gambitgen:\nMakefile:1880:\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-records.ss\nMakefile:1885:# Runs on Chez alone, so it gates in CI whether or not gambit is installed.\nMakefile:1911:gambitgencheck:\nMakefile:1912:\t@out=$$(mktemp -d)/records-gambit.ss; \\\nMakefile:1913:\t  GEN_RECORDS_OUT=\"$$out\" $(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-records.ss >/dev/null; \\\nMakefile:1914:\t  if diff -q \"$$out\" host/gambit/records-gambit.ss >/dev/null; then \\\nMakefile:1915:\t    echo \"gambitgencheck: records-gambit.ss is current with the records files\"; \\\nMakefile:1917:\t    echo \"gambitgencheck: host/gambit/records-gambit.ss is STALE — run 'make gambitgen'\" >&2; \\\nMakefile:1918:\t    diff -u host/gambit/records-gambit.ss \"$$out\" | head -40 >&2; \\\nMakefile:1923:# Gambit seed-mint gate: re-mint the gambit seed into a temp dir on Chez and\nMakefile:1924:# require it to match host/gambit/seed/ byte-for-byte. Fails when gen-seed.ss\nMakefile:1926:# chez seed was re-minted without `make gambitseed`. Runs on Chez alone, so it\nMakefile:1927:# gates in CI whether or not gambit is installed.\nMakefile:1928:gambitseedcheck:\nMakefile:1930:\t  if ! GEN_SEED_OUT_DIR=\"$$out\" $(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-seed.ss > \"$$out/mint.log\" 2>&1; then \\\nMakefile:1932:\t    echo \"gambitseedcheck: gen-seed.ss FAILED — the gambit seed cannot be minted from current sources\" >&2; \\\nMakefile:1935:\t  if diff -q \"$$out/prelude.ss\" host/gambit/seed/prelude.ss >/dev/null \\\nMakefile:1936:\t      && diff -q \"$$out/image.ss\" host/gambit/seed/image.ss >/dev/null; then \\\nMakefile:1937:\t    echo \"gambitseedcheck: gambit seed is current with the sources\"; \\\nMakefile:1940:\t    echo \"gambitseedcheck: host/gambit/seed is STALE — run 'make gambitseed'\" >&2; \\\nMakefile:1944:gambitcheck: gambitffi-bridge\nMakefile:1946:\t\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/gambitcheck.ss && \\\nMakefile:1947:\t\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 180 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-public.ss; \\\nMakefile:1953:# driven through the real natives. Same detection-gated shape as gambitcheck;\nMakefile:1955:gambitkernel:\nMakefile:1957:\t\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/kernel-test.ss; \\\nMakefile:1964:# gated like gambitcheck. In the ci list: it is the only gate that runs\nMakefile:1967:gambiteval:\nMakefile:1969:\t\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 180 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/eval-test.ss; \\\nMakefile:1976:# evals at runtime, against host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt (untaken paths;\nMakefile:1981:# after gambitboot: both regenerate boot-full.ss, and under -j a reader must\nMakefile:1983:gambitunbound: gambitboot\nMakefile:1985:\t\tJOLT_GSC=\"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" sh host/gambit/unbound-check.sh; \\\nMakefile:1990:gambitunbound-regen:\nMakefile:1991:\t@JOLT_GSC=\"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" sh host/gambit/unbound-check.sh --regen\nMakefile:1998:# died). Against host/gambit/unbound-vars-allowlist.txt; a stale line fails.\nMakefile:2000:gambitvars:\nMakefile:2002:\t\t\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/unbound-vars.ss < /dev/null; \\\nMakefile:2007:gambitvars-regen:\nMakefile:2008:\t@JOLT_GAMBITVARS=regen \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/unbound-vars.ss < /dev/null\nMakefile:2012:# host-static-methods.ss's on Chez and host/gambit/host-statics.ss's here, and\nMakefile:2016:# against host/gambit/seed-statics-allowlist.txt, a stale line fails. A grep\nMakefile:2018:gambitstatics:\nMakefile:2020:\t\tJOLT_GSI=\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" sh host/gambit/seed-statics.sh; \\\nMakefile:2025:gambitstatics-regen:\nMakefile:2026:\t@JOLT_GSI=\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" sh host/gambit/seed-statics.sh --regen\nMakefile:2031:# gates in CI whether or not gambit is installed.\nMakefile:2032:gambittwins:\nMakefile:2033:\t@sh host/gambit/eval-twins-check.sh\nMakefile:2038:# Ordered after gambitboot: gen-boot.ss rewrites boot-active.ss for every\nMakefile:2040:gambitprofile: gambitboot\nMakefile:2042:\t\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-boot.ss repl; \\\nMakefile:2043:\t\t\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/profile-test.ss; \\\nMakefile:2051:# intern) while every other gambit gate stayed green. Skipped, like the other\nMakefile:2052:# gambit gates, when gambit-scheme is absent.\nMakefile:2053:gambitboot:\nMakefile:2055:\t  $(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-boot.ss full; \\\nMakefile:2056:\t  out=$$(cd host/gambit && \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" boot-probe.scm < /dev/null 2>&1); \\\nMakefile:2058:\t    *BOOT-OK*) echo \"gambitboot: full-profile boot OK on gsi\";; \\\nMakefile:2059:\t    *) printf '%s\\n' \"$$out\" | tail -20; echo \"gambitboot: FAILED — full-profile boot did not reach BOOT-OK\" >&2; exit 1;; \\\nMakefile:2065:# ---- P1b-stage1: the gambitffi* gates ----------------------------------------\nMakefile:2069:# behind the ahead-of-time native bridge (host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm,\nMakefile:2070:# compiled by gsc into build/gambit-ffi/joltffi-bridge.o1). Blocking,\nMakefile:2075:# host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt — verified before compiling, output digests\nMakefile:2078:# runs under the P1a-r2 external watchdog (host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh, the\nMakefile:2082:GAMBIT-FFI-DIR := host/gambit/ffi\nMakefile:2083:GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD := build/gambit-ffi\nMakefile:2095:GAMBIT-FFI-SHARED-FLAGS = $(error gambitffi: unsupported fixture-link platform '$(GAMBIT-FFI-HOST-OS)' (expected Darwin or Linux))\nMakefile:2096:GAMBIT-FFI-ERRNO-ACCESSOR = $(error gambitffi: unsupported errno-accessor platform '$(GAMBIT-FFI-HOST-OS)' (expected Darwin or Linux))\nMakefile:2100:gambitffi-verify-digests:\nMakefile:2103:$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-bridge.scm \\\nMakefile:2105:\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\nMakefile:2115:\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT_GSC) $(GAMBIT_GSI) \"$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/include/gambit.h\" \\\nMakefile:2116:\t  \"$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/lib/libgambit.a\" > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/runtime.sha256\nMakefile:2118:$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture.c \\\nMakefile:2120:\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\nMakefile:2127:$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c \\\nMakefile:2129:\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\nMakefile:2139:$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt \\\nMakefile:2141:\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\nMakefile:2150:# bridge + fixtures, always current: the entry every gambitffi gate depends on\nMakefile:2151:.PHONY: gambitffi-force gambitffi-verify-digests\nMakefile:2152:gambitffi-force:\nMakefile:2154:gambitffi-bridge: gambitffi-verify-digests $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 \\\nMakefile:2159:gambitffi-abi: gambitffi-bridge\nMakefile:2161:\t\tJOLT_FFI_ERRNO_ACCESSOR=\"$(GAMBIT-FFI-ERRNO-ACCESSOR)\" sh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-abi.ss && \\\nMakefile:2162:\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 180 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-public.ss; \\\nMakefile:2175:gambitffi-errno-check: gambitffi-bridge $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test/joltffi-bridge.o1\nMakefile:2177:\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-errno.ss; \\\nMakefile:2182:gambitffi-load-failure-smoke: gambitffi-bridge\nMakefile:2184:\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 90 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-load-failure.ss; \\\nMakefile:2190:gambitffi: gambitffi-abi gambitffi-errno-check gambitffi-load-failure-smoke\nMakefile:2191:\t@echo \"gambitffi: PASS — all stage-1 qualified-tier gates green\"\nMakefile:2197:#   make gambitweb GAMBIT_WEB_OUT=../jolt-lang.github.io/resources/static/js/jolt-web.js\nMakefile:2199:# PROFILE selects how much of the language the bundle carries (host/gambit/\nMakefile:2205:GAMBIT_WEB_OUT ?= target/gambit/jolt-web.js\nMakefile:2206:gambitweb:\nMakefile:2208:\t\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-boot.ss $(PROFILE); \\\nMakefile:2211:\t\t(cd host/gambit && \"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" -target js -exe -o \"$$out\" repl-main.ss); \\\nMakefile:2212:\t\techo \"gambitweb: $(GAMBIT_WEB_OUT) ($$(wc -c < \"$$out\" | tr -d ' ') bytes,\\\nMakefile:2219:# seed ON CHEZ with the backend target at :gambit (R9), grep-verifying the\nMakefile:2220:# emission contains no chez-only spelling before writing host/gambit/seed/.\nMakefile:2221:# Runs on CHEZ (gambitseed), not gsi.\nMakefile:2222:gambitseed:\nMakefile:2223:\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-seed.ss\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Provenance checks with synthetic files/host metadata, not Linux ABI tests.\"\"\"\nimport contextlib\nimport io\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\n\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\nimport toolchain\n\nINPUTS = (\"bin/gsi\", \"bin/gsc\", \"bin/gambuild-C\", \"include/gambit.h\",\n          \"lib/libgambit.a\", \"lib/libgambitgsi.a\", \"lib/libgambitgsc.a\")\n\n\nclass ToolchainChecks(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        temporary = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=os.environ.get(\"TMPDIR\"))\n        self.addCleanup(temporary.cleanup)\n        self.root = Path(temporary.name)\n        self.prefix = self.root / \"install\"\n        self.records = self.root / \"records\"\n        self.records.mkdir()\n        for name in INPUTS:\n            path = self.prefix / name\n            path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n            path.write_bytes((\"synthetic input: \" + name).encode())\n        self.linux = SimpleNamespace(sysname=\"Linux\", machine=\"x86_64\")\n        self.record = self.records / \"TOOLCHAIN.linux-x86_64.sha256\"\n\n    def invoke(self, action, host=None):\n        out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n        with patch.object(toolchain, \"MANIFEST_DIR\", self.records), \\\n                patch.object(toolchain.os, \"uname\", return_value=host or self.linux), \\\n                contextlib.redirect_stdout(out), contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):\n            code = toolchain.main([action, str(self.prefix)])\n        return code, out.getvalue(), err.getvalue()\n\n    def valid_record(self):\n        self.record.write_text(toolchain.render_manifest(self.prefix, \"linux-x86_64\"))\n\n    def test_record_and_accept_linux_manifest(self):\n        with patch.object(toolchain.subprocess, \"run\") as refresh:\n            code, out, err = self.invoke(\"record\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 0, err)\n        self.assertIn(\"platform=linux-x86_64\", out)\n        self.assertIn(\"manifest=host/gambit/ffi/TOOLCHAIN.linux-x86_64.sha256\", out)\n        self.assertIn(\"recorded 7 toolchain inputs\", out)\n        refresh.assert_called_once_with([\"sh\", str(self.records / \"make-digests.sh\")], check=True)\n        lines = self.record.read_text().splitlines()\n        self.assertEqual(lines[:2], [\"# joltffi toolchain manifest v1\", \"# platform: linux-x86_64\"])\n        self.assertEqual(tuple(line.split(\"  \")[1] for line in lines[2:]), INPUTS)\n        code, out, err = self.invoke(\"verify\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 0, err)\n        self.assertEqual(out.count(\": OK\\n\"), 7)\n\n    def test_missing_linux_manifest_never_falls_back_to_darwin(self):\n        (self.records / \"TOOLCHAIN.darwin-arm64.sha256\").write_text(\n            toolchain.render_manifest(self.prefix, \"darwin-arm64\"))\n        code, out, err = self.invoke(\"verify\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 1)\n        self.assertIn(\"TOOLCHAIN.linux-x86_64.sha256\", out)\n        self.assertIn(\"missing toolchain manifest\", err)\n\n    def test_changed_binary_is_rejected(self):\n        self.valid_record()\n        (self.prefix / \"bin/gsc\").write_bytes(b\"changed binary\")\n        code, _, err = self.invoke(\"verify\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 1)\n        self.assertIn(\"bin/gsc: FAILED\", err)\n\n    def test_mislabelled_platform_is_rejected(self):\n        self.record.write_text(toolchain.render_manifest(self.prefix, \"darwin-arm64\"))\n        code, _, err = self.invoke(\"verify\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 1)\n        self.assertIn(\"header mismatch\", err)\n\n    def test_incomplete_duplicate_or_extra_inputs_are_rejected(self):\n        lines = toolchain.render_manifest(self.prefix, \"linux-x86_64\").splitlines()\n        for rows in (lines[:-1], lines[:3] + [lines[2]] + lines[4:], lines + [lines[-1]]):\n            with self.subTest(rows=rows):\n                self.record.write_text(\"\\n\".join(rows) + \"\\n\")\n                code, _, err = self.invoke(\"verify\")\n                self.assertEqual(code, 1)\n                self.assertIn(\"seven ordered inputs\", err)\n\n    def test_unrecorded_platform_is_rejected(self):\n        code, out, err = self.invoke(\"verify\", SimpleNamespace(sysname=\"FreeBSD\", machine=\"amd64\"))\n        self.assertEqual(code, 1)\n        self.assertIn(\"platform=freebsd-x86_64\", out)\n        self.assertIn(\"missing toolchain manifest\", err)\n\n    def test_record_is_deterministic_and_install_path_independent(self):\n        second = self.root / \"other-install\"\n        shutil.copytree(self.prefix, second)\n        os.utime(second / \"bin/gsc\", (0, 0))\n        self.assertEqual(toolchain.render_manifest(self.prefix, \"linux-x86_64\"),\n                         toolchain.render_manifest(second, \"linux-x86_64\"))\n\n    def test_missing_input_does_not_replace_existing_pins(self):\n        self.valid_record()\n        before = self.record.read_bytes()\n        (self.prefix / \"bin/gsi\").unlink()\n        with patch.object(toolchain.subprocess, \"run\") as refresh:\n            code, _, _ = self.invoke(\"record\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 1)\n        self.assertEqual(self.record.read_bytes(), before)\n        refresh.assert_not_called()\n\n    def test_invalid_platform_key_is_rejected(self):\n        code, _, err = self.invoke(\"verify\", SimpleNamespace(sysname=\"../Linux\", machine=\"x86_64\"))\n        self.assertEqual(code, 1)\n        self.assertIn(\"invalid uname platform key\", err)\n\n    def test_unindexed_manifest_is_rejected_by_full_verifier(self):\n        # Exercise the actual shell entry points in an isolated checkout slice.\n        destination = self.root / \"checkout/host/gambit/ffi\"\n        shutil.copytree(Path(toolchain.__file__).parent, destination)\n        record = subprocess.run([\"sh\", str(destination / \"record-toolchain.sh\"), str(self.prefix)],\n                                capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20)\n        self.assertEqual(record.returncode, 0, record.stdout + record.stderr)\n        verify = [\"sh\", str(destination / \"verify-digests.sh\"), str(self.prefix)]\n        good = subprocess.run(verify, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20)\n        self.assertEqual(good.returncode, 0, good.stdout + good.stderr)\n        (destination / \"TOOLCHAIN.unindexed.sha256\").write_text(\"unreviewed pins\\n\")\n        bad = subprocess.run(verify, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20)\n        self.assertNotEqual(bad.returncode, 0)\n        self.assertIn(\"catalog is stale\", bad.stderr)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main(verbosity=2)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
